  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/Kebechet/Blazor.EventHandlers.ShortClick",
  "published": "2026-11-23T18:07:59.493Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Added an opt-in click mode: with data-shortclick-mode=\"click\" on <html>, <body> or any element, a click that a pointer made reaches the page only when its press was a short click, so a plain @onclick behaves like @onshortclick. A press held for 400ms or longer, or moved past the threshold, loses its click and the click's default action. Keyboard and programmatic clicks always pass, and text-entry controls are exempt. Off by default; @onshortclick is unchanged. Also added data-shortclick-long-press-ms: how long a press may be held and still be a short click (default 400ms), for @onshortclick and click mode alike, from the nearest element carrying it; a value that is not a positive number falls back to 400. Fixed: a press is timed by its events' own timestamps, so a quick tap released while the main thread is busy (a WebAssembly render) is no longer taken for a long press; every pointer is tracked on its own, one gesture raises at most one shortclick, touch, mouse and pen presses are tracked apart, and a cancelled press is forgotten.",
